{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-substrate-consistency-window-interpretation","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:substrate-consistency-window-interpretation","kind":"remark","title":"Falsifiability of the substrate consistency window","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-substrate-consistency-window"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-substrate-consistency-window","tags":["substrate-parameter","falsifiability","consistency","interpretation"],"text":"substrate-consistency-window-interpretation.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:substrate-consistency-window-interpretation\"></a><p><strong>Significance.</strong>\nThe overdetermination of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> acts as a stringent test of the framework. Three independent measurement classes agree on the identical parameter. The consistency window <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[1.109, 1.112]</code> remains narrow (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta q / q \\approx 0.3\\%</code>) and tightens with observational precision. Any future measurement falling outside this window falsifies the framework.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/substrate-consistency-window-interpretation.md","heading":"Remark","number":"17.1.3","page":"b/rem-substrate-consistency-window-interpretation","qa":{"counts":{"pass":60,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":17,"unknown":0,"stale":49},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
